virglrenderer: end transform feedback with its own program bound

What: a stream-output target the guest destroys while its transform feedback is
still paused on the host (Mesa's virgl driver unbinds the targets to end, the GL
object stays paused) is ended with the program the recording began with bound,
and the previous program restored. Recordings also end when that program is
destroyed and when the sub-context goes away, so glDeleteTransformFeedbacks never
sees an active object. A draw that binds the same targets again with another
program or primitive ends the old recording and begins a new one instead of
resuming (GL refuses such a resume, which lost the whole context).
Why: Apple's GL reads the current program in glEndTransformFeedback. vrend binds
no program for clears and transfers, so after a readback the end dereferenced
NULL (SIGSEGV at 0x40 in glEndTransformFeedback_Exec): any guest app could crash
QEMU. dEQP-GLES3.functional.transform_feedback.* (12 of 27 sampled cases) and
WebGL 2 conformance2/transform_feedback did. With another program bound the end
failed with GL_INVALID_OPERATION and the context was lost.
Upstream: upstreamable (the NULL program is a GL spec grey zone, but ending with
the begin program is correct everywhere); not sent.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-transform-feedback.c (build time, 15 teardown orders on
Apple's GL; without this patch, on the whole gpu-robust series, cases 3, 5, 7,
11, 14 and 15 crash with SIGSEGV; with it all 29 checks pass);
tests/graphics: ./deqp.sh gles3 --filter 'transform_feedback' and ./webgl.sh
--version 2.0.0 --filter '^conformance2/(transform_feedback|vertex_arrays)/'.
